    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0655" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.111/77.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 1, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The stores of Ottoman Syrians, and those of Syrians of other nationalities who
                    have not received licenses, were officially closed to-day. <pb facs="0656"
                        n="540" xml:id="pg540"/> Two Americans were affected by this action, but the
                    Haitian Government yesterday promised that their stores would not be closed and
                    it is probable that adjustment in regard to them can be made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Furniss</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
